{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792717654,"nonce":"X9GESyfhzP/jjppwDyQHdQOQUBE=","message":"Linux and macOS CI both fail build_macros_load_helpers_and_their_macro_only_dependencies because Xml uses StringBuf, whose bundled runtime implementation calls rayzor.Bytes.alloc. That native extern is unavailable in the macro host. Stock Haxe eval declares StringBuf as a core extern supplied by its host.\n\nThe proposed bundled-library conditional was removed entirely, including the stored-length workaround. The compiler now supplies macro StringBuf construction, methods, and length reads independently of stdlib source. The optional bytecode path defers these objects to the macro host and excludes their target bodies from compiled class morsels. End-to-end LSP coverage exercises native manifests and ordinary hxml projects; unit coverage exercises native bodies, rejecting target bodies, and stock eval-style extern declarations, including Unicode and shared aliases.","files":null}]}